<%# The inbox. Subscribed to the viewer's inbox stream: new activity anywhere
    triggers a Turbo 8 page refresh (morphing, scroll-preserving), which
    re-renders this page per-viewer — see Chats::Broadcasts for why refreshes
    beat surgical row patches here.

    Two panes (`config.inbox_layout = :split`, the default): the list in a
    <nav> on the left, and on the right the `chats_conversation` frame with
    the open conversation (/messages/:id renders this same template, see
    ConversationsController#show) or the empty pane (/messages). chats.css
    decides with one media query: at least 700px wide both panes show; below
    that the page is the list (/messages) or the thread (/messages/:id), as
    with `:stacked`, which renders the list alone and the thread on its own
    page (show.html.erb). Every request renders the same markup; only CSS
    knows the width, so it works before JavaScript runs and without it.

    A row is a real link to /messages/:id. On a wide screen it targets the
    frame: the server answers with the pane alone (pane.html.erb) and the
    frame's data-turbo-action="advance" moves the address bar and history
    there. A reload, a deep link or back/forward renders the whole page.
    The frame is `disabled` until chats--split enables it, and only while
    the screen is wide: on a phone, and without JavaScript, the same link
    opens the thread page. The pane keeps its draft, scroll and stream
    through every refresh of the list (see _conversation_pane).

    Rows come from Chats::Inbox and are either a Chats::Conversation or a
    Chats::InboxGroup (every direct thread with a `inbox: :grouped` messager,
    stacked into one row).

    The chats--refresh-inbox wrapper heals a MISSED refresh broadcast: Action
    Cable has no replay, so a broadcast sent while the socket was down (tab
    backgrounded, network blip) would leave the inbox stale until the user
    navigated. The controller re-runs the same page refresh when the stream
    reconnects, when the page comes back after 10 seconds hidden, when the
    network comes back and when the browser restores the page (see
    chats/recovery.js), and reruns a refresh Turbo dropped because it
    arrived mid-visit. It wraps the <turbo-cable-stream-source> that
    `turbo_stream_from` renders: the stream's own confirmations are how it
    sees a reconnect. One per page: don't wrap it in a reconciler of your
    own as well. %>

<%# The OTHER inbox-staleness case, distinct from a missed broadcast: a Turbo
    RESTORATION visit (browser back / Hotwire Native stack pop) serves the
    inbox's cached snapshot with no GET. Open a chat from a profile, send a
    message, tap back — the snapshot cached before the chat existed comes back
    and the new conversation is missing until you navigate away and return.
    The wrapper above can't help (it fires on reconnect and visibility, not
    on a restore visit). `turbo-cache-control: no-cache` makes the inbox
    uncacheable, so a restore visit re-fetches from the network and is always
    fresh — on the web AND in Hotwire Native, whose back-pop issues a Turbo
    `.restore` visit that honors this. Requires the host layout to
    `yield :head` (the Rails convention); harmless no-op otherwise.
    https://turbo.hotwired.dev/handbook/building#opting-out-of-caching %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <meta name="turbo-cache-control" content="no-cache">
<% end %>
<%= chats_styles %>
<div data-controller="chats--refresh-inbox">
  <%= turbo_stream_from chats_current_messager, :chats_inbox %>
</div>

<% split = chats_two_panes? %>
<% inbox_empty = @rows.none? && params[:q].blank? %>
<% list = capture do %>
  <header class="chats-inbox__header">
    <h1 class="chats-inbox__title"><%= t("chats.inbox.title") %></h1>
  </header>

  <% if @inbox.filtered? %>
    <p class="chats-inbox__filter">
      <%= t("chats.inbox.filtered_by", name: Chats.display_name_for(@inbox.with)) %>
      <%= link_to t("chats.inbox.clear_filter"), conversations_path, class: "chats-inbox__filter-clear" %>
    </p>
  <% end %>

  <% if Chats.config.search && !@inbox.filtered? %>
    <%# No `action` (so a bare tag.form: form_with always writes one): a form
        without one submits to the page's own URL (the HTML standard, and
        Turbo too), whatever that is NOW — /messages,
        /messages/ (the engine answers both), or /messages/:id after a row
        opened a conversation in the pane and moved the address bar. So the
        URL a search puts in the address bar is still this page to Turbo,
        the next refresh morphs it instead of re-rendering it from scratch,
        and on the two-pane page the open conversation stays open. %>
    <%= tag.form method: :get,
          class: "chats-search",
          role: "search",
          data: {
            controller: "chats--debounced-submit",
            action: "input->chats--debounced-submit#queue search->chats--debounced-submit#queue",
            "chats--debounced-submit-delay-value": 250,
            turbo_frame: "chats_inbox_results",
            # The query goes in the URL (replaced, not pushed): a page
            # refresh re-requests the URL, so a live update or a catch-up
            # keeps the results and the field as they are.
            turbo_action: "replace"
          } do %>
      <%= search_field_tag :q, params[:q],
            placeholder: t("chats.inbox.search_placeholder"),
            class: "chats-search__input",
            autocomplete: "off" %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>

  <%= turbo_frame_tag "chats_inbox_results", target: "_top" do %>
    <%# Slot: anything the host wants above the first row — a support door,
        an announcement, a filter bar. Renders only when the partial exists. %>
    <%= chats_slot :inbox_top, viewer: chats_current_messager, inbox: @inbox %>

    <% if @rows.any? %>
      <ul class="chats-inbox__list">
        <% @rows.each do |row| %>
          <% if row.is_a?(Chats::InboxGroup) %>
            <%= render "chats/conversations/group", group: row, viewer: chats_current_messager,
                                                    pane: split, current: @conversation,
                                                    filter: chats_inbox_filter %>
          <% else %>
            <%= render "chats/conversations/conversation_row",
                  conversation: row,
                  viewer: chats_current_messager,
                  unread_count: @unread_counts.fetch(row.id, 0),
                  pane: split,
                  current: @conversation,
                  filter: chats_inbox_filter %>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    <% elsif params[:q].present? %>
      <div class="chats-empty">
        <p class="chats-empty__title"><%= t("chats.inbox.no_results_title") %></p>
        <p class="chats-empty__hint"><%= t("chats.inbox.no_results_hint", query: params[:q]) %></p>
      </div>
    <% elsif !split %>
      <%# (Two panes: the empty pane says it, once — chats/conversations/_empty_pane.) %>
      <div class="chats-empty">
        <span class="chats-empty__icon" aria-hidden="true">💬</span>
        <p class="chats-empty__title"><%= t("chats.inbox.empty_title") %></p>
        <p class="chats-empty__hint"><%= t("chats.inbox.empty_hint") %></p>
        <%= chats_slot :inbox_empty, viewer: chats_current_messager, inbox: @inbox %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>

<%# data-chats-dock-hide: the messaging dock hides itself on this page. %>
<% if split %>
  <%= tag.div class: "chats chats-inbox chats-split",
              data: {
                chats_dock_hide: true,
                controller: "chats--split",
                action: "turbo:before-prefetch->chats--split#prefetch " \
                        "turbo:frame-load->chats--split#opened " \
                        "turbo:before-morph-attribute->chats--split#keepEnabled"
              } do %>
    <nav class="chats-split__list" aria-label="<%= t("chats.inbox.title") %>" data-chats--split-target="list">
      <%= list %>
    </nav>

    <%= turbo_frame_tag Chats::ConversationsController::PANE_FRAME,
          class: "chats-split__conversation",
          target: "_top",
          disabled: true,
          data: { turbo_action: "advance", "chats--split-target": "frame" } do %>
      <% if @conversation %>
        <%= render "chats/conversations/conversation_pane",
                   conversation: @conversation, participant: @participant,
                   messages: @messages, more: @more_messages, first_unread_id: @first_unread_id,
                   counterpart: chats_counterpart, read_pending: @read_pending %>
      <% else %>
        <%= render "chats/conversations/empty_pane", inbox_empty: inbox_empty, inbox: @inbox %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
<% else %>
  <div class="chats chats-inbox" data-chats-dock-hide>
    <%= list %>
  </div>
<% end %>
